# Documentation site build output
/docs-site/book/
/_site/

# `kiln build x.kiln` with no -o writes the module name into the current
# directory, which is how three ELF binaries came to be committed. Ignore
# extension-less files at the root — every real one has a suffix or lives in a
# subdirectory. The re-includes must come before the directory rules below, or
# `!/*/` un-ignores /vendor/ and sweeps 1900 vendored files into a commit.
/*
!/*.*
!/*/
# ...but `!/*.*` re-includes every dotted name at the root, which brings back
# the build products the rules above already excluded. A stray `main.ll` from
# `kiln emit` is untracked-but-not-ignored without this, and fifteen of them
# once accumulated at the root of a working tree.
/*.ll
/*.o
/*.s
# Workflow scratch scripts, which are session artefacts and not part of the
# project. `!/*.*` would otherwise re-include them for the same reason.
/.wf-*.js

# Directory ignores, restated AFTER the root rule above so it cannot override
# them. Git applies the last matching pattern, so order is load-bearing here.
/build/
/dist/
/target/
/scratch/
/tmp/
/vendor/
/docs-site/book/
/_site/
/designer/kiln-designer
